## Vercel Web Analytics Implementation

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for this static HTML website.

### What Was Implemented

This project is a **static HTML website** without a JavaScript framework or package manager. Following the official Vercel documentation for static HTML sites, I added the Vercel Web Analytics script to all HTML pages.

### Changes Made

**Modified Files (10 total):**
- `index.html` - Main landing page
- `choix-esperluette.html` - Choice page
- `option1.html` through `option6.html` - Six option pages
- `optionb.html` - Additional option page B
- `optionc.html` - Additional option page C

**Change Details:**
Added the following script tag just before the closing `</body>` tag in each HTML file:
```html
<script defer src="https://cdn.vercel-insights.com/v1/script.js"></script>
```

### Implementation Approach

1. **Fetched Latest Documentation**: Retrieved the most up-to-date installation instructions from https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart
2. **Identified Project Type**: Confirmed this is a static HTML site (no framework, no package.json)
3. **Followed Static Site Instructions**: For static HTML sites, Vercel requires manual script injection rather than NPM package installation
4. **Applied Consistently**: Added the analytics script to all 10 HTML pages in the project

### How It Works

- The script is loaded with the `defer` attribute, ensuring it doesn't block page rendering
- The script URL points to Vercel's CDN at `cdn.vercel-insights.com`
- Once deployed to Vercel, analytics will automatically start tracking page views and web vitals
- Data will be available in the Vercel dashboard under the Analytics tab

### Next Steps

To enable analytics in production:
1. Deploy these changes to Vercel
2. Navigate to your project dashboard on Vercel
3. Go to the Analytics tab
4. Enable Web Analytics if not already enabled
5. Analytics data will start appearing after users visit the site

### Notes

- No package installation was required since this is a static HTML site
- No build step verification was needed (no build process)
- No dependencies or lock files to update
- The implementation follows Vercel's recommended approach for static HTML sites
- All existing code structure and functionality has been preserved
